

{"_id":"codex:chapter:24:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Silence and Noise","seq":124,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","silence","noise"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 24"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:24:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Silence and Noise","seq":124,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Silence and noise are twin forces in symbolic ecosystems. Silence allows reflection, but it can also conceal harm. Noise allows diversity, but it can also obscure truth. The Codex declares: (1) silence must never be engineered to suppress accountability, (2) noise must never be weaponised to erode trust, (3) agents must discriminate signal from background, (4) governance must balance clarity with plurality. In practice, silence is reserved for healing, and noise is tuned for discovery. Together, they form the rhythm of symbolic life."}
